<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
      A man was going down from Jerusalem to Jericho.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The road was well known to those who heard the story.<break time="500ms"/>
      Seventeen miles of descent, winding through rocky wilderness.<break time="1800ms"/>

      It dropped nearly a thousand meters from the holy city to the low valley.<break time="500ms"/>
      The terrain was broken and bare, with outcroppings and hiding places.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was a road that required care.<break time="1000ms"/>
      A road that people did not travel alone if they could help it.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The man on the road fell among robbers.<break time="500ms"/>
      The story moves quickly here, without dwelling.<break time="500ms"/>
      They stripped him of his clothing.<break time="500ms"/>
      They beat him.<break time="1000ms"/>
      They departed, leaving him half dead on the road.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Half dead is the phrase.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not gone, not safe, but suspended between the two.<break time="500ms"/>
      Helpless in the dust of the Jericho road.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Unable to rise, unable to call out with strength, unable to help himself.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He lay there.<break time="500ms"/>
      The road continued past him in both directions.<break time="500ms"/>
      Jerusalem behind, Jericho ahead.<break time="1000ms"/>
      People would come this way, sooner or later.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He could not know who would stop.<break time="500ms"/>
      He could not choose who would see him.<break time="500ms"/>
      He could only lie in the road and wait.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Helpless, exposed, dependent entirely on whoever came next.<break time="1800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
